I am freezing in my thin jacket.
I walk quickly into my apartment building.
Fortunately, it is very warm here.
My neighbor Nina is standing out in the hallway.
"Hi Maya," says Nina with a smile.
"How is it going?" she asks.
"Hi Nina," I say.
"It is going fine, but I miss my family today."
Nina looks kindly at me.
I show a bag from a supermarket.
"I have a tea and a cake," I explain.
"I am calling my mother and my father now."
"Is your family in Mexico?" Nina asks.
"Yes, they are in my home country," I answer.
"That sounds like a cozy call," says Nina.
"Good evening to you and your family," she says.
"Thank you very much," I smile.
I open my door and go inside.
